<title>CHILE: Chilean economy grows 5.8 pct in December.</title>
<headline>Chilean economy grows 5.8 pct in December.</headline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Chilean economy grew by 5.8 percent in November over the same month in 1995, as measured by the Monthly Indicator of Economic Activity, or Imacec, the Central Bank reported.</p>
<p>The growth rate was slightly below most market expectations. It was down from 7.7 percent in October 1996 and from 9.2 percent in November 1995.</p>
<p>((--Roger Atwood, Santiago newsroom +56-2-699-5595 x211))</p>
